# Public Servers
Servers other people run, each read through the Spell `spell place ingest` wrote for it, untouched:  each a page of its own.
GitHub's is first, then Open Library's, then JSONPlaceholder's, which takes writes, then Open-Meteo's, the weather, then the Met Museum's artworks, then REST Countries', every country.

<spell-app "public servers">
	<spell>
		- its "tab" is text
		- its "library" is a new open library page
		- its "weather" is a new open meteo page
		- its "museum" is a new met museum page
		- its "atlas" is a new rest countries page
		- to create it:
			set its tab to "github"
	</spell>

	<action "show (server as text)">
		set its tab to server
	</action>

	<draw>
		<toolbar appearance="secondary pointing" aria-label="Servers">
			<item active={its tab is "github"} onClick={show "github"}>GitHub</item>
			<item active={its tab is "open library"} onClick={show "open library"}>Open Library</item>
			<item active={its tab is "jsonplaceholder"} onClick={show "jsonplaceholder"}>JSONPlaceholder</item>
			<item active={its tab is "open meteo"} onClick={show "open meteo"}>Open-Meteo</item>
			<item active={its tab is "met museum"} onClick={show "met museum"}>The Met</item>
			<item active={its tab is "rest countries"} onClick={show "rest countries"}>REST Countries</item>
		</toolbar>
		<if its tab is "github">
			draw (a new github page)
		<otherwise if its tab is "open library">
			draw its library
		<otherwise if its tab is "jsonplaceholder">
			draw (a new jsonplaceholder page)
		<otherwise if its tab is "open meteo">
			draw its weather
		<otherwise if its tab is "met museum">
			draw its museum
		<otherwise if its tab is "rest countries">
			draw its atlas
		</>
	</draw>
</spell-app>


# What a book and a city can do, from anywhere
Only this file can name the public servers:  so its other files ask this.

<spell>
	to open (a book):
		set the public servers' library's showing to it

	to pick (a city):
		set the public servers' weather's city to it
</spell>
